('2024:holy-water', '2024', 'Holy Water', 'gear', 'Adventuring Gear', null, false, 2500, 1, null, null, 'When you take the Attack action, you can replace one of your attacks with throwing a flask of Holy Water. Target one creature you can see within 20 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 plus your Dexterity modifier and Proficiency Bonus) or take 2d8 Radiant damage if it is a Fiend or an Undead.', null),
('2024:horn', '2024', 'Horn', 'tool', 'Musical Instrument', null, false, 300, 2, null, null, '', null),
('2024:hunting-trap', '2024', 'Hunting Trap', 'gear', 'Adventuring Gear', null, false, 500, 25, null, null, 'As a Utilize action, you can set a Hunting Trap, which is a sawtooth steel ring that snaps shut when a creature steps on a pressure plate in the center. The trap is affixed by a heavy chain to an immobile object, such as a tree or a spike driven into the ground. A creature that steps on the plate must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw or take 1d4 Piercing damage and have its Speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. Thereafter, until the creature breaks free of the trap, its movement is limited by the length of the chain (typically 3 feet). A creature can use its action to make a DC 13 Strength (Athletics) check, freeing itself or another creature within its reach on a success. Each failed check deals 1 Piercing damage to the trapped creature.', null),
